
{0 OCaml TIFF}

OCaml TIFF is a library for working with TIFF
(Tagged Image File Format) images in OCaml.

It provides functionality for reading and writing
TIFF images and accessing image metadata.

{1 Getting started}

- {{:https://github.com/geocaml/ocaml-tiff#readme}README}
  — Introduction and installation instructions.
- {{:https://github.com/geocaml/ocaml-tiff/tree/main/examples}Examples}
  — Example programs demonstrating library usage.
- {{:https://github.com/geocaml/ocaml-tiff/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md}Contributing}
  — How to build, test and contribute.

{1 Library [tiff]}

The library provides APIs for working with TIFF
images and their associated metadata.

- {!module:Tiff} — Main interface for working
  with TIFF files.
- {!module:Tiff.Ifd} — Access TIFF Image File
  Directory (IFD) metadata.

{2 File access}

The file access types describe how TIFF data
is read from and written to files.

- {!type:Tiff.File.ro} — Read-only file access.
- {!type:Tiff.File.wo} — Write-only file access.

{1 Supported TIFF functionality}

The following functionality is available through
the library.

{2 Reading TIFF images}

The {!module:Tiff} module provides functionality
for reading TIFF images.

See {!Tiff.from_file} for creating a TIFF value
from a file.

{2 Image dimensions}

TIFF image dimensions are stored in Image File
Directory (IFD) entries.

- {!Tiff.Ifd.width} — Retrieve the image width.
- {!Tiff.Ifd.height} — Retrieve the image height.

{2 TIFF metadata}

The {!module:Tiff.Ifd} module provides access
to TIFF Image File Directory metadata.

See the module documentation for the available
metadata accessors.

{2 GeoTIFF metadata}

GeoTIFF extends TIFF with geospatial metadata.

The {!module:Tiff.Ifd} module contains functions
for accessing supported GeoTIFF information.

